Z||000010||Sillhouette.com||06-05-2000||05:57 PM||||Yeah I do see the difference and that is that my fiero with the mods is much more than 140 HP and 160 ft lbs.  Also I have a lot of junk shielding cruise control and extra wiring off my fiero.  That is I beat the guy.  He did have a jump on me half way through the intersection.  I don't know if that is reaction time or slightly higher torque.  The end result was still the same. My fiero was half car length in front when we applied brakes.<P>Cheers<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>Fiero <BR>140 hp - 160 ft lbs thq 2600 lbs - 3000 lbs<BR>Mustang 5.0<BR>225 hp - 300 ft lbs thq 2700 lbs - 3200 lbs<P>see a difference?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Haze_Performance||06-05-2000||08:08 PM||||I raced a very nice red 86-up Fiero GT (stick)in my 92 Mustang GT Droptop (auto).<BR>It was a light to light race. It didnt even hang with me.(But he kept tring  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )||||reg||10
Z||000012||Dan86gt3.8||06-06-2000||12:20 PM||||Well, I beat a auto rag top pretty handely.  Then I raced a friend of mine which who has an 89 gt.  Its faster than other because it is speed density instead of mass air.  He has an off road H-pipe and flowmasters, ohh yeay its a T-5.  Anyways whe raced 3 times, I of course couldn't spin my tires if I wanted to.  But on the first race he beat me by like half a car by the 1/4 mile mark, the other 2 times he spun and then spun and missed second& spun.  Point is if they don't hoook up (mainly the t-5 guys) they are easy to beat.  Anyways if you can find a stock AOD mustang they are slow I would say as much as a second or more in the quarter.  Anyways take care and suprise stang owners, because they usually think they are awesome and sometimes they aren't <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
