Z||000014||87PegasusGT||06-06-2000||06:43 PM||||I'll buy that, but the carburated 350s in the 1980 Z28s weren't as fast the Tune Port Injected 5.0 Rustangs either.||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||06-08-2000||08:38 AM||||sorry.. I've got LOADS AND LOADS of mods done to my car... and off the bottle i can KEEP UP... if they are not really paying attn I can pull 1/2 car lenght to the next ligh... HOWEVER! on the bottle they don't stand a chance... the Fiero traction is far better than the moostangs and whiles hes smoking his tires your already stoped at the next light waiting! The Fiero is a better light to light car than a 1/4 mile car... if you really have to pick a fight with a mustang just make sure there is at least one corner.. you'll SMOKE him around the corner and then you have a fighting chance. The FOX body cars are great cars but probly 80% of the guys that race then are Drag guys with drag suspension setup which don't have the geometry for any decent cornering... Our cars will hold over 1g in a corner and in acceleration...! with no real difficult work. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||1FST2M6||06-08-2000||08:50 AM||||Sillhouette... where do you live?  check <A HREF="http://www.dynojet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dynojet.com</A>  see if there is a dyno center near you and have your car run... see what it's really laying down.  Not saying your cars not fast, but it's nice to know what your up aginst. ||||reg||1
Z||000017||BBBAD GT||06-08-2000||09:50 AM||||The way I read it is if 5.0 guy wants to race a Fiero, then its a given the 5.0 is pretty much stock.  Trust me, the only stock early 5.0's out there anymore are ones that grandma and grandpa drive.  But, just like the Fiero, as they age, the miles pile up.  <P>In my opinion, a 5.0 guy with a low 13 sec potential or better wouldn't even bother a guy in a Fiero unless provoked (no disrespect to the Fiero), but thats just me.  They would rather save up for a LS-1 or C5.  Then of course, there's the 16 yr old kid who just bought a ragged out 5.0 who wants to race anything that moves. That I can't stand!!<P>    ||||reg||1
Z||000018||1FST2M6||06-08-2000||12:30 PM||||theres LOTs of those annoying kids around here... either just getting their car or "dads out of town he'll never notice the miles" it's funny... they all pick fights but when they lose they all go home right after that... MUCH like the RICER flyby huumm strange... You being a Blue oval owner know what it's capable of and don't waste your gas... these kids are just TRYING to be cool... adaquitly powered car and toss a girl or friends/audiance into the mix.. and yep.. you've got a street race. the difference between an enthusist and a gimp kid. -when you DO meet a real car at a light and pick a fight with your stock looking car AND hold your own they will stop and talk to ya instead of sticking their tail between there legs and run home- <P>example...  Friday night sitting at the  Coffee Shop on the main"drag" Barret Parkway. I installed a nitrous kit on a buddies 4dr B16a1 Civic(4 days prior). after a little fiddeling with the jet selection we finally got the torque we were looking for. hes out causing trouble and meets a white SN95 at a light the driver of the White Mustang gives him the "i'm gunna wipe the floor with you" stab of the throttle just to let my friend know he's got a S/C... the whine could be heard for couple hundred feet. Dave (my friend not being affraid) taps the nitrous purge... to alert the other driver what he's up aginst, readys his car at about 1500 the light turns the nitrous solenoids pop and they both leave in a cloud of exspelled unburnt fuel. about 1.8th mi later they both are off the throttle and headed into the area I was at. After a brief razzing of the mustang owner about owning one.. they met for the first time and are cordual.. no lame flyby, no cheesy fart can "i'm a lame A$$, and won't stop cause i lost" clutch drop. just two enthusists altho in different classes both on the same plane.    Sounds like good ending for a car romance novel!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     for those interested the 4dr. Civic has a Jap Spec B16a1 (DOHC VTEC) with an 85 shot of Nitrous and the SN95 had an Vortech 9psi S/C. (of course the normal H-pipe change and Pro-Flo (not flowmaster) 2.25" exhaust and BBK headers & bigger injectors)  just my $.02||||reg||1
Z||000019||My7Fieros||06-08-2000||03:54 PM||||Hmmm, I hate to be different than everyone else..but let me say this: I was in my 86 Se V6 4 speed, some guy in a newer body (sn95)mustang gt was giving me "whatever" look and was getting froggy at a light. Now Im not just saying this because of my fondness for Fieros, but we jumped on it at the green light..he got me for about the first 2 or 3 seconds, then he was about maybe a car length behind me...for quite some time! By the time we made it to the next light, he looked at me with this "what the hell have you got in that thing" look. I must admit, I felt really good! Then I felt better when I showed him my badge, (Im a cop..hehe!)and he took it much slower off the line the next time! ;-)||||reg||7
